ted by plant.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","japan","ceramic","japanese-art","meiji-period-1868-1912"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.29},"sw":"#929292","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2022.158/2022.158_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2369":{"n":2369,"cl":102,"id":"cma-447765","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Sweets Bowl","creator":"Seifū Yohei III","date":"1893–1914","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2022.195"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Names for the glazes, written in ink with a brush on the lids of the custom-made storage boxes for the works, often indicate a specific glaze or ware that had inspired Seifū Yohei III.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["19th-century","japan","ceramic","japanese-art","meiji-period-1868-1912","glazed-porcelain"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.29},"sw":"#898886","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2022.195/2022.195_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2370":{"n":2370,"cl":102,"id":"cma-447759","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Vase with Plum Blossoms","creator":"Seifū Yohei IV","date":"1914–46","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2022.211"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Yohei IV’s allover design of budding and flowering plum blossoms, strongly associated with spring and with China, is combined with his father’s “water color” glaze on this vase.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["20th-century","japan","ceramic","japanese-art"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.29},"sw":"#8f908f","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2022.211/2022.211_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"en