ypical of vessels of this era, so archaeologists named the period after them.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["ancient","japan","ceramic","japanese-art","500-300-bce"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.25},"sw":"#a4a2a2","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1998.32/1998.32_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2888":{"n":2888,"cl":102,"id":"cma-380089","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Flat Dish Made of Marbled Clay","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"960–1234","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2020.187"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This dish features lively contrasting black and beige clay marbling underneath a transparent glaze.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["medieval","ceramic"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"sw":"#8b8b8b","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2020.187/2020.187_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2892":{"n":2892,"cl":102,"id":"cma-97532","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Jar","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1522–66","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1917.13"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The jar with brilliant cobalt blue decoration depicts the four seasons and stages in the life of a scholar-official.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["16th-century","ceramic","china","jiangxi-province","ming-dynasty-1368-1644","jingdezhen-kilns"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"sw":"#242323","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1917.13/1917.13_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2949":{"n":2949,"cl":102,"id":"cma-125995","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Ewer with a Lion-shaped Spout","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"900s–1000s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1948.220"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This remarkable ewer is most likely a very early and rare type of Yaozhou ware, with the shape and decoration recalling Tang metal ware. High quality pieces like this might have been sent as tribute to the Northern Song court.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["medieval","ceramic","china","shaanxi-province","yaozhou-ware","tongchuan"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"sw":"#5e6167","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1948.220/1948.220_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2976":{"n":2976,"cl":102,"id":"cma-171614","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Tea Whisk-Shaped Sake Bottle","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1660s–early 1670s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2014.391"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This bottle is for sake, or fermented rice wine, Japan's most famous variety of local alcohol.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["17th-century","japan","ceramic","edo-period-1615-1868","japanese-art","early-iro-e"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"sw":"#414242","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2014.391/2014.391_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2977":{"n":2977,"cl":102,"id":"cma-299304","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Dish with Maple Leaves in Waves","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"late 1600s–early 1700s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2017.62"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"This pottery type was named for the Nabeshima family, who established kilns to produce highly refined porcelain meant for diplomatic gifts.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["17th-century","japan","ceramic","edo-period-1615-1868","japanese-art","nabeshima-type"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.25},"sw":"#3d3d3d","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2017.62/2017.62_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"2978":{"n":2978,"cl":102,"id":"cma-380090","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Large Bowl with Molded Decoration","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1300s–1400s","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2020.188"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Longquan celadon, or greenware, was often fired in dragon kilns, a type of narrow, sloped brick tunnel that could fire up to 25,000 pieces at a time.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["14th-century","ceramic","china","porcelaneous-stoneware","zhejiang-province","longquan-kilns"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.25},"sw":"#484848","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2020.188/2020.188_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"3001":{"n":3001,"cl":102,"id":"cma-140179","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Libation Cup in the Form of a Jue","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1662–1722","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1964.177"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"The handle is decorated with a dragon mask, while the body has a fret pattern in the incised underglaze.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["17th-century","ceramic","china","jiangxi-province","jingdezhen","qing-dynasty-1644-1911"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.25},"sw":"#3f3f3d","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1964.177/1964.177_web.jpg","fallback":null,"pos