 ceramic might not be your choice for a pillow, it actually kept the user cool as they slept.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["ceramic","china","11th-century","jiangxi-province"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.25},"sw":"#4c4d52","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2003.88/2003.88_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"3165":{"n":3165,"cl":102,"id":"cma-169191","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Double-chambered Vessel with Figures and Camelid","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"1470–1532 (Thermoluminescence date, 1310–1610)","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2011.112"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"When this vessel is filled with liquid and tilted back and forth, the camelid emits a whistling sound.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["15th-century","ceramic","aa-andes","andes","chim-inka"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"sw":"#3f3f3f","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2011.112/2011.112_web.jpg","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"3168":{"n":3168,"cl":102,"id":"cma-159722","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Figure in a Litter","creator":"Unknown maker","date":"500–900 (Thermoluminescence date, 590–1090)","source":{"institution":"Cleveland Museum of Art, Open Access","work":null,"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1997.1"},"rights":{"license":"CC0"},"editorial":{"note":"Whether a deity, ancestral mummy, or masked human, this figure signals power. The divided eyes and fangs are traits of supernatural beings.","noteSource":"source","room":"interiors","tags":["medieval","ceramic","aa-andes","middle-horizon","wari-pachacamac-style","epoch-2"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.25},"sw":"#58504a","media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1997.1/1997.1_web.jpg","fallback":null,